  "text": "Subscribe to skip adsAdvertisementTechnologyHuman Vision Has Quirks That AI Can’t MatchYour robot butler can’t do a Magic Eye poster… yetKFBy Kristen French1:00 PM CDT on October 6, 2026Add Nautilus to GoogleHuman vision is imperfect. Our eyes do not always represent the world exactly as it is. We have blind spots. We see after-images. We are tricked by optical illusions. But some of these imperfections may be adaptive features of biological vision rather than flaws.Powered By 10 ShareNextStayToday’s AI vision systems are imperfect in a different way. They are very good at accurately mapping an object in physical space, but they can’t reproduce the ways that picture might be altered by the human visual experience.  Read more: “How Your Brain Fills in the Blanks with Experience”Subscribe to skip adsAdvertisement",
